+# Agent Self-Improvement Loop
+
+This repository includes a controlled loop that lets the agent propose
+changes to its own `skills/`, `prompts/`, and `workflows/` — and nothing
+else — under strict, isolated, evaluated, audited, human-gated control.
+
+Start here: **[evolution/README.md](evolution/README.md)**.
+
+Quick map:
+
+| Concern | Location |
+|---|---|
+| What the loop may/may not touch | `policy/self_improvement_policy.json` |
+| Who may approve | `auth/approvers.json` |
+| Automated gates (schema/regression/holdout) | `evals/` |
+| Orchestrator CLI | `evolution/self_improve.py` (or `evolution/bin/self-improve`) |
+| Promotion + one-command rollback | `deployment/` |
+| Immutable audit trail | `audit/changes.jsonl` |
+| CI-level defense in depth | `.github/workflows/self-improvement-guard.yml` |
+
+`policy/`, `security/`, `auth/`, `evals/`, `evolution/`, `deployment/`,
+and `audit/` are the trusted control plane: the loop must never modify
+any of them. Only `skills/`, `prompts/`, and `workflows/` are ever
+proposed as changes.
