+# evals/
+
+The evaluator for the agent self-improvement loop — the gate every
+proposed change must clear before a human is even asked to look at it.
+
+- `evaluator.py` — runs all three gates against an isolated worktree and
+  fails closed (any gate failing fails the whole change).
+- `schema/validate_frontmatter.py` — structural validation of touched
+  skill/prompt/workflow files (offline, deterministic, no model calls).
+- `regression/` — known-good behavior (`cases.json`) that must not break.
+- `holdout/` — cases never used while developing a change, to check it
+  generalizes rather than overfitting to the regression set.
+
+Both `regression/run_regression.py` and `holdout/run_holdout.py` ship
+with a static keyword/marker proxy check by default, so the gate runs
+fully offline. To wire in real behavioral grading (actually invoking the
+agent against each case's `query` and grading the transcript), set the
+`SELF_IMPROVE_GRADER_CMD` environment variable to a command that reads a
+case as JSON on stdin and exits 0 for pass / nonzero for fail.
+
+For a genuine holdout guarantee in production, move `holdout/cases.json`
+to a store the proposing agent has no read access to at all, and have
+only the evaluator (running in a trusted context) fetch it — in this
+scaffold it's a plain file for simplicity, so it's readable, just never
+writable, by the loop.
+
+**This directory must never be modified by the self-improvement loop.**
+Only a human operator, editing outside the loop, may change the gates,
+the case sets, or the pass/fail thresholds.
