+# Controlled Self-Improvement Loop
+
+This is the harness that lets the agent propose changes to its own
+`skills/`, `prompts/`, and `workflows/` — and nothing else — under strict,
+auditable, human-gated control.
+
+## Trust boundary
+
+```
+ EDITABLE by the loop            READ-ONLY control plane (bootstrap-only)
+ ───────────────────             ──────────────────────────────────────
+ skills/                         policy/     — the safety policy
+ prompts/                        security/   — (unrelated to this system; never touch)
+ workflows/                      auth/       — who may approve
+                                  evals/      — the evaluator (schema/regression/holdout)
+                                  evolution/  — this orchestrator itself
+                                  deployment/ — promotion + rollback rules
+                                  audit/      — the append-only audit logger
+```
+
+The agent operating the loop may **edit files** only under `skills/`,
+`prompts/`, `workflows/`. It never edits files in the right-hand column —
+it only **invokes** the CLI in this directory as a tool call, and that CLI
+enforces the boundary structurally (see `policy/policy.py`): any diff that
+touches a forbidden path is rejected before a worktree is even created.
+
+This whole tree (`policy/`, `security/`, `auth/`, `evals/`, `evolution/`,
+`deployment/`, `audit/`) was created once, by a human operator, as
+bootstrap. Once bootstrapped, the self-improvement loop must never
+propose changes to any of it — only a human, working outside the loop,
+may evolve the harness itself.
+
+## Lifecycle
+
+Every proposed change goes through the same eight steps:
+
+1. **Explain the problem.** The agent states, in plain text, what
+   behavior it observed and why it's a problem. Passed as `--problem`.
+2. **Unified diff.** The change is expressed as a standard unified diff
+   against the current trunk, touching only `skills/`, `prompts/`,
+   `workflows/`.
+3. **Apply only in an isolated git worktree.** `propose` creates a fresh
+   worktree + branch under `.evolution-worktrees/` and applies the patch
+   there — the primary working tree is never touched at this stage.
+4. **Run regression and holdout evaluations**, plus a schema/structural
+   check, against the isolated worktree (`evals/evaluator.py`).
+5. **Reject if any gate fails.** Fail-closed: one failing gate rejects
+   the whole change, no partial credit. The worktree is torn down.
+6. **Record the result** in `audit/changes.jsonl` — proposals, rejections,
+   approvals, promotions, and rollbacks all get one line each,
+   append-only.
+7. **Require explicit human approval** before promotion. `approve` checks
+   the approver against `auth/approvers.json`; `promote` re-checks it and
+   additionally requires the promoter to be the same human who approved.
+8. **One-command rollback.** `deployment/rollback.sh <approver-id>`
+   reverts the trunk to the immediately-prior promoted commit.
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# 1-5. Propose a change (fails closed on policy or eval gate failure)
+evolution/bin/self-improve propose \
+  --problem "The X skill fails to activate on trigger phrase Y" \
+  --diff /path/to/change.patch
+
+# 6. Inspect what happened
+evolution/bin/self-improve list
+evolution/bin/self-improve show --change-id chg-20260824-153000-ab12cd
+
+# 7. A human reviews the worktree printed by `propose`, then approves
+evolution/bin/self-improve approve --change-id chg-... --approver operator
+
+# Promotion (only the approving human, only after approval)
+evolution/bin/self-improve promote --change-id chg-... --approver operator
+
+# 8. Roll back to the previous promoted version, any time, one command
+deployment/rollback.sh operator
+```
+
+## Why this can't be talked out of its guardrails
+
+- **Policy check runs before disk I/O.** `policy/policy.py` inspects the
+  diff's touched paths (parsed straight out of the unified diff, not
+  taken from the proposal's own claims) before a worktree exists.
+- **Isolation is structural.** `git worktree` gives every proposal its
+  own working directory and branch; nothing merges into trunk without an
+  explicit `promote`.
+- **Fail-closed evaluation.** Any one of schema / regression / holdout
+  failing rejects the whole change.
+- **The audit logger only appends.** `audit/logger.py` has no update or
+  delete function — the trail can't be quietly edited.
+- **Approval requires a real human identity.** `auth/approvals.py`
+  rejects `agent`/`self`/`bot`/`ci`/`system` outright, and fails closed if
+  `auth/approvers.json` is empty.
+- **CI re-checks independently.** `.github/workflows/self-improvement-guard.yml`
+  doesn't trust this CLI's exit code — it re-derives the touched-path set
+  and re-runs the eval gates at the PR boundary.
+- **The harness can't modify itself.** Every module the loop depends on
+  for its own safety (`policy/`, `auth/`, `evals/`, `evolution/`,
+  `deployment/`, `audit/`) is itself outside the set of paths the loop is
+  allowed to propose changes to.
